        "code": {
          "text": "Emerging mild erectile dysfunction concerns"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported back pain characteristics"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "New gradual-onset mid-to-lower central back pain, slightly right-sided, for approximately 5–6 days, with no clear injury or radiation to the legs. Dull, tight ache, 4–5/10 at baseline and up to 7/10 after a big work day."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Back pain timing, aggravating and relieving factors"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Worse at the end of the day while working on concrete and first thing in the morning; eases somewhat after moving. Aggravated by bending, lifting ladders and tools, prolonged standing, driving on a rough farm track, and possibly a new firmer mattress and increased ute driving on a rough driveway. Relieved by lying flat, a heat pack, and Nurofen."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Back pain red-flag symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "By history, denies trauma or fall; saddle anaesthesia; leg weakness or numbness; bowel or bladder incontinence or urinary retention; fever, night sweats, weight loss, or unrelenting nocturnal pain. No known cancer or systemic illness."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Back pain impact and reported mobility"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Still working and pacing himself, avoiding heavy lifting, and has not taken time off. Reports mobilising okay and being able to heel-toe walk, squat, and climb stairs."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Telehealth examination limitations and observed presentation"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Telehealth by phone; physical examination was not possible. Speech coherent and engaged, asking appropriate questions, and in no distress over the phone."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Peyronie's disease history and curvature"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Diagnosed approximately 12 months ago in association with penile curvature and a palpable plaque. Curvature reported as about the same over the last few months. Previously under intermittent review; no surgery and no specific Peyronie's treatment tried."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported erectile and penile symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild erectile symptoms described as 'takes a bit more effort'; denies complete erectile dysfunction. Some discomfort with intercourse. Denies penile pain at rest, haematuria, dysuria, and discharge. Has not tried a PDE5 inhibitor."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Targeted neurological, urinary, and constitutional symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies limb weakness, paraesthesia, and gait disturbance. Urinary stream normal; denies frequency or urgency and reports no change in baseline nocturia of once nightly. Denies unexplained weight loss, fever, and fatigue except fatigue related to poor sleep from pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported medical history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Known Peyronie's disease. Reports no other significant known chronic disease and no known diabetes or cardiovascular disease."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/MedicationStatement/medication-statement-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "MedicationStatement",
        "id": "medication-statement-1",
        "status": "active",
        "medicationCodeableConcept": {
          "text": "Ibuprofen (Nurofen)"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "dosage": [
          {
            "text": "400 mg twice daily as needed; used for the last 3 days",
            "asNeededBoolean": true,
            "timing": {
              "repeat": {
                "frequency": 2,
                "period": 1,
                "periodUnit": "d"
              }
            },
            "doseAndRate": [
              {
                "doseQuantity": {
                  "value": 400,
                  "unit": "mg"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "note": [
          {
            "text": "Reported partial relief."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/MedicationRequest/medication-request-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "MedicationRequest",
        "id": "medication-request-1",
        "status": "active",
        "intent": "order",
        "medicationCodeableConcept": {
          "text": "Ibuprofen"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "dosageInstruction": [
          {
            "text": "Continue 400 mg three times daily as needed with food, for up to 5–7 days if tolerating gastrointestinally.",
            "asNeededBoolean": true,
            "timing": {
              "repeat": {
                "frequency": 3,
                "period": 1,
                "periodUnit": "d"
              }
            },
